# auditor-api

Paths relative to `apps/auditor-api/`. Payloads: `@cloudpulse/api-contracts`. Mocks: mock-data-style.

- **Topology & Ingress**: Co-located inside single AWS VPC on ECS Fargate (ARM64 / Graviton). Zero public IP / zero internet ingress. Ingress accepts traffic on port `3333` exclusively from Next.js web portal Security Group.
- Thin controllers: route, extract, call service, return. No business logic in controllers.
- `CLOUD_AUDITOR_SERVICE` & Header Routing: `AppController` inspects `x-cloudpulse-mode` header sent by Next.js BFF. When `mode === 'demo'`, `AppController` selects `MockCloudAuditorService`; otherwise it routes to `AwsCloudAuditorService` (`applyLiveAwsEnv` + AWS SDK clients in `src/auditor/` using `resolveLiveAwsProfile()`).
- No ORM and no Repository layer. AWS SDK lives in auditor services.
- Validate request bodies `@Body()` at the controller with contract Zod (`safeParse`), throwing Nest `BadRequestException` on failure.
- Use Nest `HttpException` subclasses (`BadRequestException`, …). Do not add a global exception filter unless one is introduced on purpose.
- MCP SSE lives in `src/mcp/` (`propose_terraform_remediation_pr`).
- Tests: Jest, colocated `*.spec.ts`.
